      "notes": { "design": "The ring is four Fort Ring quarters (kit tiles: a wall 1.6 m thick and 3.6 m high, 15 m to its middle from the fort's centre, firing slits at eye height) round a 2 x 2 keep: gates at the south-west, south-east and north-west (where the courtyard is narrowest, 2.9 m to the keep's corner, so nobody sees straight in), the north-east quarter whole. The keep's ground floor is the command room, big enough for a final hold zone (6 m round its middle stays inside it and under its ceiling), with two doors south and one west and slits east and west; over it the radio room (north-west) and a roof terrace behind parapets that sees over the ring, reached by a stair along the keep's north wall from the courtyard. It can't be mirrored (the ring's quarters are L-shaped): turn it so its gates face the attack." }
